def node(i,k,c):graph['nodes'].append(dict(id=i,kind=k,contract=c,qualified_id=None,compiled52=False,proof_body_expanded=False,formal_status='UNIMPLEMENTED_INTERNAL_SOURCE_OBLIGATION' if k=='authored-internal-obligation' else 'SOURCE_ONLY_BOUNDARY'))
def edge(a,b,k='source-mathematical-ingredient',r='Necessary internal mathematical obligation; not a public certificate premise or compiled call',span=None):
 d=dict(id='E52.'+str(len(graph['edges'])),ingredient=a,consumer=b,kind=k,reason=r,compiled52call=False)
 if span:d['source_span']=span
 graph['edges'].append(d)
obligations={
 'H52.input':'Exactly sealed binders: finite real Hilbert/Borel E (rank0 allowed), probability mu, eta>0, real signed C1 compact f. No moment, density, positivity normalizer, derivative, domination, closure or bound premise.',
 'O52.bounds':'Derive continuous f and continuous actual fderiv, actual compact support of fderiv, then nonnegative global Mf,Mdf bounds (take max(C,0)). No caller constants.',
 'O52.normSym':'For all x,y, norm(x-y)=norm(y-x). Identify the literal target tilt exponential with parent kernel, everywhere.',
 'O52.affine':'phi_y(x)=2*x-y is continuous measurable for every y; parameter derivative D_y phi=-id. All real scalar-module typing is inferred from genuine Hilbert structure, including zero dimension.',
 'O52.gaussian':'K(y,x)=exp(-norm(y-x)^2/(2eta))>0, K<=1. Actual D_yK=-(K/eta) scalar-multiply innerSL_R(y-x). Derive via norm-square, exponential, chain and affine rules; no Gaussian derivative certificate.',
 'O52.gaussianBound':'Put r=norm(y-x), t=r^2/(2eta). r<=1+r^2 and t exp(-t)<=exp(-1)<=1 yield r K<=1+2eta; innerSL_apply_norm gives norm(D_yK)<=b_eta=(1+2eta)/eta. True in rank0; do not use Nontrivial-only innerSL_norm.',
 'O52.integrand':'F(y,x)=f(2*x-y)*K(y,x). Actual derivative G(y,x)=-K(y,x) scalar-multiply fderiv_R f(2*x-y) - (f(2*x-y)*K(y,x)/eta) scalar-multiply innerSL_R(y-x). Both negative signs genuine. NormF<=Mf, normG<=Mdf+Mf*b_eta.',
 'O52.typing':'E and its real continuous-linear-functional space have actual finite-dimensional metrizable/separable typing, real Banach target and real normed scalar action. These internally discharge the neighborhood/first-countability/strong measurability/CLM integral contracts; no extra class hypothesis.',
 'O52.meas':'From genuine continuous f, fderiv and Gaussian/affine maps derive F(y,.) and G(y,.) strongly/AES measurable for every y; G(.,x) continuous for every x. Also f strongly measurable for map integral. These are real analytic obligations, not arbitrary versions.',
 'O52.L1':'Probability mu supplies finite measure; constant Mf and B=Mdf+Mf*b_eta are integrable. Actual AES+global pointwise bounds give F(y,.) and G(y,.) L1 and K(y,.) L1 for every y, without any moment hypothesis.',
 'O52.Nderiv':'N(y)=integral F(y,x) dmu. For each y0 use s=univ (one genuine neighborhood independent of x), actual AES, F(y0) L1, G(y0) AES, B L1, and all-x/y actual derivatives to produce HasFDerivAt N (integral G(y0,x)dmu) y0.',
 'O52.NprimeCont':'Use the same global constant B and real G measurability/parameter continuity in CLM-valued continuous_of_dominated. The actual derivative field Nprime(y)=integral G(y,x)dmu is continuous.',
 'O52.NC1':'C1 characterization combines all-y actual derivatives with actual continuous Nprime to give C1N, not just Differentiable N.',
 'O52.ZL1':'Parent literal Z(y)=integral K(y,x)dmu is actual nonnegative finite real mass (K positive and <=1, mu probability). Positive parent C*Z rules out Z=0; combined with integral nonnegativity gives Z>0. This needs no caller C positivity and no law/limit certificate.',
 'O52.ZC1':'The opaque parent produces C2Z at exact eta and mu. Internally lower derivative order to C1 via ContDiff.of_le; use exact actual Z, not an existential surrogate.',
 'O52.posterior':'Actual tilted definition gives R_y=mu.withDensity(ofReal(K/Z)); positivity and real L1 normalization internally imply probability R_y and true measurable reflected map gives probability S_y. Law probability is internally derived, no new public certificate. Normalization calculation is an obligation, not a theorem output credit.',
 'O52.meanIdentity':'Every y: integral f(u) dS_y = integral f(2*x-y) dR_y = integral (K(y,x)/Z(y))*f(2*x-y) dmu = N(y)/Z(y). Use actual measurable map, strongly measurable f, literal integral_tilted, scalar integral extraction and norm symmetry. No AE replacement of laws.',
 'O52.meanC1':'Actual C1N, actual C1Z and all-y Z>0 give C1(N/Z). Substitute the everywhere identity to obtain exact sealed target.',
 'O52.zeroSign':'Signed f and zeros allowed throughout norms/products; no positivity/centering of f. In rank0 actual Z=1 and literal mean constant, derivative zero; no positive dimension or Nontrivial E premise.',
 'R52.gibbsAdapter':'LATER TYPED RESIDUAL: For actual paper mu=volume.tilted(-V), internally produced positive finite ZV and exp(-V) L1, affine u=2x-y, volume Jacobian2^-dim, tilt composition/normalization must prove literal generic S_y equals actual50 source volume-tilt S_y EVERY y. No AE uniqueness derivative transport and no pointwise-law certificate premise.',
 'R52.graphConsumer':'LATER TYPED RESIDUAL: After genuine pointwise same-S function identity, transfer C1 to actual50 literal Tf; combine actual50 two genuine Lp representatives and actual51 same-nu closable graph with c1_in_closed_gradient. Current52 gives neither adapter nor graph membership.',
 'R52.rough':'UNCLAIMED SOURCE GAP: C1 of compact-test means plus closed compact gradient is not yet full rough allL2->H1/B13. Same-nu approximation and actual weighted graph convergence still required; Gamma/halfturn/main/querycost excluded.',
}
